{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793382419704169001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"suppletive-curative-bug","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"160812f8cb123c8213314d175814695a0a9b9eab4fefaa51b992bc35529736dc","event_uuid":"8d643ecc-ac5f-476e-a202-4943180bfb41","position":{"commit_sha":"2350843cbd4f9ff62b460dc3df20a3f2ece9d4f1","position":"1793376509780768927-8d643ecc-ac5f-476e-a202-4943180bfb41"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793376509780768927,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## What happens\n\nWhen `gerrit_safe_submit.py` receives HTTP 409 from the revision-scoped submit\nendpoint, it reports the refusal without the response body Gerrit returned. The body\ncarries the reason — a merge conflict, an unsatisfied submit requirement, a\nRebase-If-Necessary failure, or a genuinely newer patch set — and those demand\ndifferent responses from the caller.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n409 is the one status where the correct next action is not inferable from the status\nalone. Without the body the caller has to open the change in a browser to learn\nwhether to rebase, wait for a vote, or resolve a conflict. In an agent session that is\na dead end, because the body is the only place the distinction exists.\n\n## Change\n\nInclude Gerrit's response body in the error output on any non-2xx submit response, not\nonly 409. Strip the `)]}'` prefix if present so the body reads as JSON, and keep the\nexisting status line so the output is a superset of today's.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** On a stubbed 409 whose body carries a `message` field, the script's\n      stderr contains that message text verbatim.\n- [ ] **AC2** The stderr also still contains the HTTP status code, so the output is a\n      superset of today's.\n- [ ] **AC3** A body prefixed with `)]}'` is printed with that prefix removed.\n- [ ] **AC4** A body that is not JSON is printed as-is rather than raising.\n- [ ] **AC5** The exit code on 409 is unchanged from today's.\n- [ ] **AC6** Unit tests cover AC1-AC5 against stubbed responses, with no network access.\n- [ ] **AC7** `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe abbreviated-SHA guard defect in the same script, tracked separately. This change\nmust not alter which revisions the guard accepts.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"84be-e805-3816-4e90","ticket_type":"bug","title":"gerrit_safe_submit.py drops Gerrit's response body on a failed submit","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8d643ecc-ac5f-476e-a202-4943180bfb41"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793382419704169001,"uuid":"5cdea6fb-db6f-4ad6-bb3a-f3aca2c3d111"}